Original commit body from 7d9b8b23c8ec068609834630a8bd6e00c3623e3a:

Audit-findings 0018 established that Symbol.kind's vocabulary is sound —
`class` is not apex/peer overloaded; abstract-ness rides on
Symbol.modifiers — and that the real defect is a missing PREDICATE: 138
values on one flat axis, so symbol_kinds_on_axis() cannot express "the
abstract types" and every consumer writes a literal instead.

SymbolKindSpec now carries type_family (abstract_type for
interface/trait/protocol; concrete_type for class/struct/enum/record/
object/union/contract), with type_like_kind_names(),
abstract_type_kind_names() and is_abstract_type(kind, modifiers) as the
Symbol.kind analogue of edge_types_on_axis(). NOT a new axis under
ADR-0024: no IR field changes, no value reclassified, so nothing touches
stable_id or the v9/v10 scheme sequencing.

Measured behaviour change. type_hierarchy gated virtual dispatch on
`child_kind == "interface"` — one of three inherently-abstract kinds —
so a Swift protocol produced `implements` and NO dispatches_to, while
the byte-equivalent Java interface produced both. That gate is now
is_abstract_type(...), which also reaches `abstract class` via the
modifier. End-to-end, Swift goes from no dispatch edge to
`dispatches_to: Shape.area -> Square.area`, matching Java exactly.

Four sites swept: type_hierarchy, inheritance (which held a CORRECT
abstract set at line 91 and an incorrect one at 426), _transitive_bases
(mutable-default literal -> None sentinel resolved from the registry),
and cli.py's class-meta index.

A linter prevents recurrence, with two principled exemptions rather than
an allow-list: expressions guarded by a sibling `language` comparison,
and modules whose declared depends_on languages cannot produce the
missing kind. That second rule is what separates a defect from a correct
set — jackson_dispatch and kafka_streams_dispatch declare
depends_on=[["java"]] and omit trait/protocol CORRECTLY, while
type_hierarchy declares scala/rust/swift and its omission is the bug. Of
eleven literals the naive rule flagged, exactly five are real defects.
The backing kind->language map carries a written R10 re-eval trigger.

Non-vacuity: the linter has a planted-offender test, plus tests for each
exemption, so a green live tree cannot pass because the walker is broken.

